# Security policy

## Reporting a vulnerability
Write to <security contact: email or private issue form>. Do not open a public issue. We
acknowledge within 72 hours and share a fix or mitigation plan within 14 days.

## Supported versions
Only the latest release (and `main`) receives security fixes.

## What this project does by design
- Threat model in `docs/security/threat-model.md` (STRIDE, lethal trifecta, OWASP LLM/Agentic).
- Secrets never live in the repository: full-history scan with gitleaks in CI and a pre-commit hook;
  `.env` is ignored and `.env.example` documents the variables.
- Dependencies are reviewed before being added (`rumbo verify-dep`), audited in CI (`pip-audit`,
  `bandit`), pinned by the lockfile and updated by Dependabot with a cooldown.
- CI never holds a model credential; `make check` is offline.
{{#llm}}
- Everything the model returns is validated against a schema; tool output and retrieved content are
  data, never instructions; tools are typed and least-privilege; rendered output carries no remote
  links or images.
{{/llm}}
- Agents cannot change the sensors (CI, Makefile, hooks, anti-cheat sensor) on their own: see
  `.claude/settings.json` and `.github/CODEOWNERS`.
